From a796d946d0d2590c4b0554c8939cc1e8afccce3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:02:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: Dreadwatch, threat domains on their own page under
 Warden

Reviewer feedback: name blocking and address blocking are different
enforcement points, and a block whose effect cannot be measured cannot be
trusted. The Warden page's threat-domain card moves to a new tab,
Warden > Dreadwatch: tiles (blocked lookups, names, devices, last update,
not recorded), the feeds table with per-feed counts and last good download,
the most-blocked names and devices (named through ReaperNames), the recent
blocked lookups, Test now, Reset counters, a coverage card (DNS Director,
the DoH canary) and the never-block names. Warden keeps one line pointing
there. Everything rendered as text.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
